# Plan: Configurable Page Size for Submission Lists (#3045)

## Approach

Add a per-source page-size preference stored in `localStorage`, surfaced as a
small dropdown in `ShowCandidatesComponent`. The selected value feeds directly
into the existing `this.pageSize` field that `performSearch()` already reads,
so no new search path is needed.

The current effective page size in `ShowCandidatesComponent` is 20 for all
entry points — set by callers via `[pageSize]` (from URL params or hardcoded),
with the base class fallback of 12 never reached in practice. There is no
existing difference between list and search. Going forward we introduce a user-controlled preference with a single shared
option set for both source types, while keeping the `@Input() pageSize` typed
to only accept valid values:

| Options      | Default |
|--------------|---------|
| 20, 50, 100  | 20      |

A single option set eliminates the need for separate list/search arrays and
any source-type branching in the preference logic. All existing callers (which
pass 20) remain valid with no changes required to caller files.

No backend changes required — `pageSize` is already part of every paged
request (`PagedSearchRequest`). No virtual scroll, no infinite scroll; full-DOM
rendering is acceptable up to 100 rows.

