### 2. `show-candidates.component.html`

Add a page-size selector alongside the existing results-summary block.
Currently (around line 280) the summary reads:

```html
<!-- Results summary for searches -->
<div *ngIf="!isSavedList()" ...>
  <div class="d-flex flex-grow-1 justify-content-end">
    <div class="text-end">
      <span>{{results?.totalElements}} candidates returned</span><br/>
      <span class="small">{{timestamp | date: 'customDateTime'}}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

Replace the outer `<div>` (which is currently `*ngIf="!isSavedList()"`) with a
layout that always shows the page-size control and conditionally shows the
count. The SavedList case currently shows nothing here, so this is non-breaking:

```html
<div class="d-flex align-items-baseline flex-wrap-reverse justify-content-between pb-3">

  <!-- Page-size selector (always visible) -->
  <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 text-muted small">
    <label class="mb-0">Per page:</label>
    <ng-select class="tc-select"
               [items]="pageSizeOptions"
               [searchable]="false"
               [clearable]="false"
               [ngModel]="pageSize"
               (ngModelChange)="onPageSizeChange($event)">
    </ng-select>
  </div>

  <!-- Results count (searches only) -->
  <div *ngIf="!isSavedList()" class="d-flex text-muted small">
    <div class="text-end">
      <span>{{results?.totalElements}} candidates returned</span><br/>
      <span class="small">{{timestamp | date: 'customDateTime'}}</span>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>
```

**Placement rationale:** Between the filter controls and the table, where
pagination concerns naturally live. Users see it before scrolling to the bottom
pagination control.

